#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "318d38c5-d3fb-52bf-8a88-5592f8301f89" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Acceleration of a Particle at a Given Moment Given Its Velocity Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c36679ec-d687-5e56-b976-cfac53665ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347195} {:answer/id #uuid "9dad882a-a310-5568-84a7-f53fd42e33f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨3,\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347196} {:answer/id #uuid "1d3a132f-25a5-5bf7-afa1-8da607228a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347197} {:answer/id #uuid "21fd382a-22ba-5c24-9097-373376910b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨4,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347198} {:answer/id #uuid "e72f3e49-2d09-5108-91cb-8ef8d18440f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨11,\\sqrt{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d3a132f-25a5-5bf7-afa1-8da607228a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(4)=⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347197} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e18736b-841d-5062-bb69-3c86541b8c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f86f6880-2810-590a-a6b3-f2816b5d8154" :question/math-academy-id "q-121908" :question/problem "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3t-1,\\sqrt{2t+1}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=4.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2t+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=4,$ we substitute $t=4$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(4) & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2(4)+1}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "380357c3-4914-5137-9449-0e02076cb248" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acceleration Vector of a Particle Given Its Position Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4227cabc-59d9-5286-984b-9cd00248c30b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347202} {:answer/id #uuid "45880911-8170-51f3-8d9d-11976c063c97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-3{t}^{2},2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347203} {:answer/id #uuid "06070c3c-03c8-5eb6-bc5e-5ed35e412ad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-6t,4t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347204} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb8d6c8-3f2f-5717-a97d-f2279c934094" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-4t,4t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347205} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf75821-19b0-5f6b-a3e4-36505e10fa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-6t,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cf75821-19b0-5f6b-a3e4-36505e10fa5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=⟨-6t,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347206} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4a9a5f-e003-510d-b35e-8c68d5714506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13d7a5d0-065f-59fe-97e0-96a304f6f591" :question/math-academy-id "q-121931" :question/problem "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨4t-{t}^{3},2{t}^{2}+t⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-{t}^{3}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4-3{t}^{2},4t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-3{t}^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6t,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344845 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "380357c3-4914-5137-9449-0e02076cb248" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Acceleration Vector of a Particle Given Its Position Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4e3f525-260a-55e0-9f95-79f3101b7c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4e3f525-260a-55e0-9f95-79f3101b7c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344847} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e0dc915-7e53-5e77-89bb-a2bbfb0fa057" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344846} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac1ffb2d-009b-5532-a629-10e950239817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12t^2-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac1ffb2d-009b-5532-a629-10e950239817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12t^2-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344849} :answer-field/id #uuid "81366150-616c-5287-a8f2-dc0553180241" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fcffff13-cdb5-5338-a8c9-56f6f641a2ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-347193" :question/problem "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-2t,\\,{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2,\\,4{t}^{3}-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t,\\,12{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408599-c601-5c8c-96a7-da7566ba07c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Acceleration of a Particle at a Given Moment Given Its Position Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9de2f21c-6e35-5193-a53d-3a790e6bde9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de2f21c-6e35-5193-a53d-3a790e6bde9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347209} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e492577-8f3c-597b-ba0c-62eec5ca3e38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30cfb7b2-1ef0-559b-9da5-320d1575e984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30cfb7b2-1ef0-559b-9da5-320d1575e984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347211} :answer-field/id #uuid "1808fa0e-76a3-57c7-ba26-612284b512c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d8918a7-328e-53cc-86ce-67ceda4d8417" :question/math-academy-id "q-347197" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1,\\,4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=0.$ Do not round the answers.\n\n$a(0)=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4+{t}^{2}-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t,\\,2t-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-4,\\,2-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨6(0)-4,\\,2-6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186347212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17408599-c601-5c8c-96a7-da7566ba07c1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Acceleration of a Particle at a Given Moment Given Its Position Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d4599a-28d2-53e3-b499-79234ac86f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨-1,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347214} {:answer/id #uuid "5bc8ef76-2f41-5d8d-a2d6-3d805f6e3172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨0,48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347215} {:answer/id #uuid "585c8299-7145-545e-84c1-d5bdccfef4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨1,96⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347216} {:answer/id #uuid "70e28c51-ce40-5e60-860e-c8848bf21efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨0,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347217} {:answer/id #uuid "6385b3f5-eb07-5ab6-aed5-c8c27105f522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨1,48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6385b3f5-eb07-5ab6-aed5-c8c27105f522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a(2)=⟨1,48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347218} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f22f698-3cf0-5dd8-a9d7-98c5b05260ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c35299e-e7ea-52d7-8411-4ed07a1c0894" :question/math-academy-id "q-85609" :question/problem "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,3+{t}^{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3+{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2-t},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{2-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{2-t},\\,12{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨{e}^{2-2},12(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,48⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
